 "story": "Easy now. Don't let the nerves show.\n\nLeft hand steady on the wall, right hand tight on iron - count the heartbeats, listen for boots on gravel. Can't trust the silence; it's fooled better men than me. Whoever's out there, they know this alley as well as I do.\n\nOne more second, then move. Don't give - em the first shot.\n\nOut here, you only get to be surprised once.",
 "notes": "The strength of the composition comes from restraint and awareness. The narrow alley compresses space around the figure, turning the weathered boards and angled stance into a stage for anticipation. Light grazing the timber and the guarded posture of the gunman create a psychological pause that echoes the tension of classic Western cinema while maintaining the quiet authority associated with painterly photographic work.",
