 "story": "Not much in this town she hasn't seen before. \nTrouble rides in loud, but trouble always rides out quieter.\n\nShe keeps an eye on the corners, the faces, \nwaiting to see who tips their hat and who forgets. \nMost folks think they're the ones doing the watching.\n\nShe lets them. \nIt's better that way - \nafter all, even a quiet day is worth keeping a hand close to the rail.",
 "notes": "Technically, the photograph is a study in subtle power - controlled highlights on hat brim and vest, gentle diffusion at the edges, and sharpness only where it matters most: the eyes. The effect is both welcoming and defensive, embodying a character who's seen trouble, handled it, and will handle it again if need be. Collectors will find in this image a rare balance of grit and restraint - a portrait that expands the mythology of the West by centering the watchful, indomitable women who shaped it.",
